{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"739","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Recover a functional graph"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Functional graph is a directed graph in which all vertices have outdegree equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". Loops are allowed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Some vertices of a functional graph lay on a cycle. From the others we can come to a cycle by making a finite number of steps along the edges (we consider only finite functional graphs in this problem)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's compute two values for each vertex. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"precyclei"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the amount of edges we should pass to get to a vertex which is a part of some cycle (zero, if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" itself lies on a cycle), "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"cyclei"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the length of the cycle we get to."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given the information about these values for some functional graph. For each vertex you know the values "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"precyclei"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"cyclei"},{"kind":"text","text":", however, instead of some values there can be the question mark. It means that these values are unknown."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Build any functional graph that suits the description or determine that there is no such graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 300"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of vertices in the graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain two integers — "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"precyclei"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ precyclei ≤ n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":") and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"cyclei"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ cyclei ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"). There could be question marks instead of some of these values."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In case there is no solution, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Otherwise, print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them is the number of vertex to which the edge form the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th vertex go."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The vertices should be in the same order as they go in input data."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are